 "notes": "Pages 84–87 (PDF 248–251), Plate XV. Spell 23 = p. 84 rows 1–7 and p. 85 rows 1–4; Spell 24 = p. 85 rows 5–9, p. 86 rows 1–4, p. 87 rows 1–4 (stopped before 'Appendix.'). Line numerals as the brief says: Spell 23 1. (p84 r1), 2. (p84 r3), 3. (p84 r4, before χesef-tu), 4. (p84 r6, before em), 5. (p85 r1, inside urt between D21 and X1), 6. (p85 r3, before āḥā); Spell 24 1. (p85 r5), 2. (p85 r5, before nuk), 3. (p85 r7, inside beḥennu), 4. (p85 r9, before à), 5. (p86 r2, inside ḥekau), 6. (p87 r1), 7. (p87 r3, before betennu). Overlines: p84 r1 re…en and t'eṭà un; p84 r2 re-à àn; p84 r6 un…àn; p85 r2 àr ḥeka; p85 r3 neb…āḥā; p85 r5 re…en; p85 r8 whole row; p85 r9 betennu, and à ànen māχent; p86 r1 ent; p86 r2 àsk…pen; p86 r4 àrit χeperu em; p87 r2 àstu and nà (separate short line); p87 r4 ki t'eṭ. Budge's font draws several signs idiosyncratically: a tall narrow rectangle with hinge-hooks (door, coded O31) in àpu, āāt, ruṭ, qemam; a flat oblong with a small cup on top (coded R4 approx) in meḥ, āper, uārt, ṭemṭ; a low runner with curled left end and tab (U15) in un, sau, sai, χesef, uṭen, Tem. Transliterations copied with Budge's raised a in χᵃχ / χᵃχt. On p86 r2 the owl before 'em' has no transliteration of its own (merged into em)."
